-- in a branch, after the λs that bind its fields, a let standing before a λ goes under it: let
-- v = t in λ x → b is λ x → let v = t in let x' = x in b. A branch's remaining λs take the
-- arguments the eliminator is applied to, and they are read off the front of the branch; a
-- definition as it was written has such lets (a clause that names the whole matched value)
x-lo-step : (Code → Code) → Code → Code → Code
x-lo-step go t (clam b) = clam (go (x-push-app c-fuel (code-shift #0 #1 (clet t (clam b))) (cvar #0)))
x-lo-step go t b = clet t b
